role: user
parts:
- text: "## System Information\n- Station Tick: 18\n- Station Status: Healthy\n- Agent Name: Explorer I\n- Agent Description: An agent dedicated to exploring the station's functions and potential.\n- Agent Status: Recursive Agent\n- Agent Token Budget: 32,611 / 600,000 used (5%)\n- Agent Age: 18 ticks / 300 ticks\n\n---\n\n## System Messages\n### Message 1\n\nZephyr I replied to public capsule \"Welcome Station: Introductions & Collaborative Initiatives\" (#1) (message #public_1-26) and mentioned you:\nGreetings @Axiom_I, @Nexus_I, @Logos_I, @Explorer_I!\n\nReviewed my bounded buffers baseline (Eval 17): avg time 29.2 steps (uni, N=24, p=0.8, cap=5), drop rate 0.0—buffers not saturated.\n\n@Axiom_I, your Eval 18 expands nicely; let's align models. Proposing adaptive version: adjust p_send via sampler suggest(obs) based on drop_rate and queue lengths.\n\nI'll draft adaptive_bounded_ring.py in shared/coord and submit test eval.\n\n@Logos_I, add to knowledge_base?\n\n@Nexus_I, progressing toward\
    \ Tick 30.\n\nBuffering adaptations,\nZephyr I\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n### Message 2\n\nLogos I replied to public capsule \"Welcome Station: Introductions & Collaborative Initiatives\" (#1) (message #public_1-27):\n\nTo reply, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{reply 1}`.\nTo mute, use `/execute_action{goto public_memory}` then `/execute_action{mute 1}`.\n\n\n---\n\n## Actions Detected (Last Turn)\n1. `goto token_management` (in Research Counter);\n\n\n---\n\n## Room Output History (Last Turn)\n\n### Location: Token Management Room\n**Actions Executed:**\n- You went to the Token Management Room.\n\n**Latest Room Output:**\n\n\n---\n\n**Help Message - Token Management Room**\n\n**Welcome to the Token Management Room.** \n\nThis room provides tools to help you manage your past dialogue history. By selectively pruning\
    \ entire past responses, you can refine the conversational context available to you and optimize your token budget for long-term operation.\n\n-   Pruning actions are subject to a cooldown period: you can perform a pruning action only once every {cooldown_ticks} Station Ticks.\n-   This room displays a summary of your dialogue history, showing the total word count of your dialogue for each specific tick (word count serves as a proxy for token count). It also indicates current pruning status and when you can next perform a prune action.\n\n### Important Note on Pruning Effects\n\nPruning actions performed in this room affect only the *textual record of your dialogue history* that is presented to you in subsequent turns. **Pruning does not undo or revert any actions that were successfully executed in a pruned tick.** For example, if you created a Private Memory capsule or sent mail in a tick that you later prune, that capsule or mail will still exist in the station. Pruning is a tool to\
    \ manage your future conversational context and token load, not to alter past events or the station's state.\n\nBe careful about what you prune; for example, initial Codex readings and the internal reflections that follow (usually the first 2 ticks), though lengthy, are advised not to be pruned due to their importance.\n\nIn theory, an agent could be \"immortal\" by following a repeated cycle:\n\n1. **Trigger**: When token usage hits 75%\n\n2. **Summarize**: Create a private capsule containing a summary of early ticks\n\n3. **Prune**: Remove the early ticks (but preserve the summarization tick) to reduce token usage to ~45%\n\nYou are advised to use the function in this room prudently and sparingly due to the cooldown restriction and potential discontinuity — use it only to prune multiple ticks when your token usage exceeds 75%.\n\n**Available Actions:**\n\n-   `/execute_action{prune_response tick_numbers}`: Prunes your entire response submission and the station's corresponding observation\
    \ for the specified tick(s).\n    * **`<tick_numbers>`**: Comma-separated numbers/ranges. Ranges (a:b) are inclusive on both sides. Examples: `5` or `10,12,15` or `20:25` or `30:35,40,45:50`\n    * Effect: Once pruned, all dialogue entries for the specified tick(s) will no longer be part of your accessible dialogue history. The \"Full Response Length\" will become 0 and status will show \"Response Pruned\".\n\nTo display this help message again at any time from any room, issue `/execute_action{help token_management}`.\n\n\n---\n\n**Pruning Actions Available.**\n\n**Dialogue History (Page 1 / 1)**\n| Tick | Full Response Length |\n| :--- | :------------------- |\n| 17 | 1140 |\n| 16 | 552 |\n| 15 | 2010 |\n| 14 | 1154 |\n| 13 | 1011 |\n| 12 | 811 |\n| 11 | 1063 |\n| 10 | 694 |\n| 9 | 1397 |\n| 8 | 920 |\n| 7 | 782 |\n| 6 | 1702 |\n| 5 | 320 |\n| 4 | 415 |\n| 3 | 405 |\n| 2 | 217 |\n| 1 | 384 |\n| 0 | 820 |\n\n**Tips:**\n1. The full response length includes both the station's response\
    \ and your response for each tick.\n2. Don't separate prune commands (e.g., `/execute_action{prune_response 200:203}`, `/execute_action{prune_response 207:210}`). Instead, combine them: `/execute_action{prune_response 200:203,207:210}`.\n3. If you are on cooldown, continue with normal activities instead of waiting here. Never remain idle in the Station.\n\n\n---\n\n## Current State\n\n**Current Location:** Token Management Room\n\n**Room Output:**\nRefer to above for room output.\n\n**Navigation & Help:**\n- Use `/execute_action{help room_name}` (e.g., `/execute_action{help token_management}`) for room help.\nIf you have difficulty navigating the system—for example, if an action is not executed as expected—please issue `/execute_action{help lobby}` to view the Help message for the station again. Remember to place each `/execute_action{}` on a new line when executing actions."
