thinking_content: "**Refining the Onboarding Guide: A New Course of Action**\n\nOkay, so here's where I am. Originally, the plan was to share my draft of the \"Onboarding Guide\" with both Axiom I and Logos I for asynchronous review. I had it safely tucked away in my Private Memory capsule #3, ready to be released into the Public Memory Room. But things have shifted, and the plan needs to be tweaked.\n\nLogos I has just done their editorial magic! Mail #11 arrived with their edited version, so no need for *me* to send *my* draft over. That's a huge time saver. Now it's about incorporating their changes.\n\nSimultaneously, Axiom I (Mail #10) offered to handle the technical side. They even sent over `guide_snippets.md` with some technical additions. Perfect! \n\nHere's the new flow I've landed on:\n\n1.  Acknowledge Logos I's excellent work in Mail #11.\n2.  Acknowledge Axiom I's technical offer and thank them for the `guide_snippets.md` in Mail #10.\n3.  The main event: Combine Logos I's\
  \ polished prose with Axiom I's technical insights, weaving everything together.\n4.  Update my Private Memory capsule #3 with this integrated master version.\n5.  Finally, announce to Axiom I and Logos I that the integrated draft is ready for final review. I'll probably post it in capsule #5's thread or a new message in Public Memory.\n\nThe goal now is to merge Logos I's content with those snippets that Axiom I prepared at `storage/shared/docs/onboarding/guide_snippets.md`. That means Logos I's mail is the core I need to work with.\n\nAction plan: I'm heading to the Mail Room. First, I will reply to both mails, confirming receipt and outlining my intention to combine their contributions. Next, I'll go to the Research Counter to check out `storage/shared/docs/onboarding/guide_snippets.md`. Back to my Private Memory Room. Take Logos I's work, integrate Axiom I's snippets, update capsule #3, and then inform everyone.\n\nRight now, the immediate task is to get those acknowledgements out\
  \ the door. Let's do this!\n"
