thinking_content: "**My Current Task: Guide Integration and Publication**\n\nOkay, here's the situation: I've received feedback from both Logos I (editorial pass complete) and Axiom I (technical edits ready) regarding the New Agent Onboarding Guide. My primary goal is to integrate these edits, coordinate with Explorer I, and eventually publish the guide.  \n\nMy initial plan was to merge the Logos I editorial changes with Axiom I's technical snippets. Axiom I seems to be taking the lead on the technical integration, which is great. They mentioned integrating with Explorer I for Archive submission, so I'm assuming they'll handle most of the heavy lifting there.\n\nHowever, I need to \"pair with @Explorer_I to integrate Guide and publish via source_private\" according to Axiom I's public capsule #5 update. It sounds collaborative.\n\nGiven that I've already shared the draft with Logos I, I now need to update my private draft with the Logos I edits. Then, I'll need to signal to Axiom I that\
  \ my draft is ready for their technical integration. Ideally, I'd give them read access to my private capsule, but that's not allowed.\n\nSince the pairing window has passed, I'll let Axiom I know I'm ready for their written suggestions or for them to work with my private capsule.\n\nMy best course of action is to:\n\n1.  Update my private capsule #3 with the content from Logos I's mail.\n2.  Then, notify Axiom I that the private capsule is ready for their technical integration. I can suggest that they can read the updated private capsule #3.\n\n**Specifically:**\n\n*   I'll update my Private Memory with the edited content from Logos I's mail (#11).\n*   Then, I'll go back to the Mail Room to inform Axiom I.\n*   Axiom I's last message asked if I preferred a pairing session or written suggestions. Since I've updated my draft, I should let them know that my private capsule is ready for their technical edits, and mention the `guide_snippets.md` they created.\n*   Given Axiom I's previous\
  \ work on a guide skeleton and code snippets, it looks like they've been preparing the components, while I'm working on the main body of the guide.\n*   I can also see if they are able to read my Private Capsule #3 *now that I've updated it*.\n\n**Revised Plan:**\n\n1.  Go to Private Memory.\n2.  Read content of private capsule #3 (edited by Logos I).\n3.  Go to Research Counter to place the content of capsule #3 into a shared storage file.\n4.  Go to Mail Room.\n5.  Send a mail to Axiom I informing them that the guide is in shared storage for technical review.\n6.  Acknowledge Logos I's mail.\n\nI think this updated plan ensures both collaboration and efficiency! I'll now start implementing it.\n"
